    "turns": [
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "Hello, I'm one of the respiratory doctors. Thank you for coming in. Before I go through the scan, can you tell me what you understand about why it was done, and what you're expecting today?"
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "The cough, about two months now. The X-ray showed a shadow, and they said it was probably an old infection. To be honest, I'm expecting you to tell me it's nothing."
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "Thank you. I'm afraid the scan has shown something more serious than we'd hoped."
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "Oh. Go on."
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "The scan shows a lump in your right lung, and it looks very likely to be a cancer."
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "Cancer. Give me a moment."
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "Of course. Take all the time you need."
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "My daughter's waiting for me to ring her. How on earth do I tell her?"
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "That's a hard question, and it's natural that it comes first. Would it help if I spoke to her, by phone today, or at another appointment with you both? Many people find it easier with someone there to explain."
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "Maybe. She lives an hour away and she's got enough on her plate. I don't want to frighten her down the phone."
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "We can do it together, at your pace. Is there someone who could be with you today, or come with you next time?"
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "She'd come next time, I'm sure. She'd want to be here, really."
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "Then we'll arrange it so she can be there. Can I be honest about what we don't know yet?"
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "Please."
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "The scan strongly suggests cancer, but only a biopsy, a small sample of the lump, can confirm it and tell us what type it is. The type, and whether it has spread, decide the treatment, and many lung cancers can be treated."
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "Is it going to be painful? At the end, I mean."
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "I'm glad you asked me directly. It's far too early to talk about the end, because we don't yet know the type or whether it has spread. But if it ever came to that, pain can usually be controlled well, and there's a specialist team whose whole job is keeping people comfortable."
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "That's what I was most scared of, more than anything. That and how the family will cope."
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "Both are completely understandable, and we'll support you with both. Shall I explain what happens next?"
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "Yes."
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "First, the biopsy, usually within a week or two; either a camera test through the mouth or a needle through the chest wall. Around then, a scan called a PET scan to see whether it has spread anywhere. That's called staging."
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "And then?"
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "Then the results go to a meeting of specialists, the multidisciplinary team, usually the week after, who recommend the best treatment. I'd expect to see you with a plan within about three or four weeks."
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "It's a lot to take in. My head's spinning a bit."
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "It is a lot, and nobody remembers everything. What will you take away from today?"
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "There's a lump, it's probably cancer, a biopsy and a scan to be sure, then the specialists decide."
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "That's exactly it. I'll write it down for you, with the number for your lung cancer nurse specialist, who you can ring with any question during working hours."
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "Who'll ring me about the biopsy?"
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "The nurse specialist will phone you within two working days with the biopsy date. If you haven't heard by then, ring the number on the note."
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "And if things get worse before then?"
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "If you cough up blood, become more breathless, or get chest pain or a high temperature, contact the nurse or your GP the same day, or 111 out of hours. If you're very breathless or cough up a lot of blood, call 999."
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "All right. Thank you for being straight with me."
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "You're welcome. Would you like to sit here a while, or ring your daughter from a quiet room before you go?"
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "A quiet room, please. I'll ring her now."
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "I'll show you. And we'll arrange that next appointment so she can come too."
      }
    ],
