    "notes": "DVLA statement: diabetes managed by diet alone needs no notification for Group 2 (lorry) drivers; notification depends on medication, especially insulin or tablets with a hypoglycaemia risk. A clinician should confirm the wording against current DVLA guidance. The card gives no medication; with an HbA1c of 71 the GP may also consider metformin, which the script leaves to the GP. The three-month repeat interval is the script's choice, in line with usual UK practice. The father's history is invented for the family-history task."
