      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "You'd record a set of sentences on a computer with a good microphone, usually a few hundred, depending on the service. It takes a few hours altogether, but you can do it at home in short sessions of ten or fifteen minutes, over several weeks. Rest when you're tired, because tired recordings are less clear."
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "That doesn't sound too bad."
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "Most people find it manageable. But I want to be honest: some people choose not to do it, and that's a genuine choice, not a box to tick. Some find it too painful, and others would rather concentrate on now."
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "I don't know yet. What do people use it for?"
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "That's really for you to shape. What would you want a recorded voice for?"
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "My grandchildren. Reading them stories. Saying I love you to my husband the way I say it. And telling the cat off."
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "Then those are exactly the things we'd focus on: stories, your own phrases, the way you say his name. And whatever you choose, it isn't banking or nothing. You could record a smaller set of personal messages instead, called message banking. There are also good ready-made computer voices, and simple tools like alphabet boards and apps."
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "That's a relief, actually. I thought it was all or nothing."
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "Not at all. What support do you have at the moment? And who would you tell about this conversation?"
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "My husband, tonight. My sister's good. I haven't told my daughter much yet."
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "That's a lot to carry. Your specialist nurse can support you, and there's a charity helpline for people with this condition and their families. If you're feeling very low or struggling to cope, please tell us or your GP."
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "I will. So what happens now?"
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "I'll give you a leaflet and a website about voice banking to read at home with your husband. Let's say you'll decide within the next month, with no pressure either way. When you're ready, or if questions come up, ring me directly; my number is on the leaflet."
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "A month. All right."
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "And if your speech changes quickly, or you notice any trouble swallowing, contact the team sooner rather than waiting. If your breathing ever becomes difficult, call 999. Can you tell me what we've agreed?"
      },
      {
        "who": "I",
        "text": "Read the leaflet with my husband, decide within the month, and ring you. Sooner if anything changes."
      },
      {
        "who": "C",
        "text": "That's it exactly. Thank you for letting me raise this today."
      }
